<%#
# Key: tools/built_in/shell/description
# Purpose: Shell Tool description.
# Used: Included in a Tool or Tool-input specification shown to the model as the shell Tool description.
# Locals:
# - command_mode: :argv or :string.
# - timeout_default: Integer seconds used when the model does not choose a timeout.
# - timeout_maximum: Integer seconds the model may request, or nil when the timeout is fixed.
# Constraints:
# - Must render non-blank.
-%>
<% if command_mode == :string -%>
Run one shell command with /bin/sh -c in the configured workspace. Shell state such as variables and the working directory does not persist between calls.
<% else -%>
Run one executable with arguments in the configured workspace. Shell syntax is not interpreted.
<% end -%>
<% if timeout_maximum -%>
Commands stop after timeout_seconds, up to <%= timeout_maximum %> seconds; the default is <%= timeout_default %> seconds.
<% else -%>
Commands stop after <%= timeout_default %> seconds.
<% end -%>
